{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q18", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [18], "type": "지칭", "answer": 1, "text": "This is an old word that translates as \"scholar\" or \"intellectual\" in the sense of someone who exhibits all of the most admirable virtues attributed to Confucianism, especially during the Joseon Dynasty. He was presented as the ideal human being who was selfless and disciplined. So, he was held up as a model of morality for all people in the Confucian society. He was also dedicated to the prosperity of the nation in politics and philosophy. In modern Korean society, scholars are still expected to keep the spirit that such a man had. However, in reality, it is very hard to live up to such ideals.", "wordCount": 106, "reconstructionKind": "none", "reconstruction": null, "hasDeliberateError": false, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 밑줄 친 This가 가리키는 것 (정답 ① 선비). 단순 추출(영어 지문 완전), 한국어 선지 제외."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q19", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [19], "type": "지칭", "answer": 2, "text": "Greg had always loved sports that he could play on his own. When he was 14, he went to a camp for skiers. One of the best ways to stay in shape, he was told there, was cycling. At that time, his dad was trying to lose weight, so he rode 20 miles every day with his son. Soon Greg got interested in cycling, entered races for 14 and 15-year-olds, and won almost every race. He became unbeatable in the U.S. However, being number one in the U.S. didn't count for much because all the top cyclists raced in Europe. When he was 16, Greg started racing and winning in Europe. And when he was 25, he became the first non-European to win the Tour de France, the top cycling competition in the world.", "wordCount": 134, "reconstructionKind": "none", "reconstruction": null, "hasDeliberateError": false, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 밑줄 친 He[he]가 가리키는 대상이 나머지 넷과 다른 것 (정답 ② = his dad; 나머지는 Greg). 밑줄 ①~⑤ 마커 제거한 완전 지문."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q21", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [21], "type": "어법", "answer": 2, "text": "The most useful thing I brought out of my childhood was confidence in reading. Not long ago, I went on a weekend self-exploratory workshop, in the hope of getting a clue about how to live. One of the exercises we were given was to make a list of the ten most important events of our lives. Number one was: \"I was born,\" and you could put whatever you liked after that. Without even thinking about it, my hand wrote at number two: \"I learned to read.\" \"I was born and learned to read\" wouldn't be a sequence that occurs to many people, I imagine. But I knew what I meant to say. Being born was something done to me, but my own life began when I first made out the meaning of a sentence.", "wordCount": 134, "reconstructionKind": "grammar_error", "reconstruction": {"kind": "grammar_error", "blankFilledWith": null, "order": null, "insertedAt": null, "insertedSentence": null, "removedSentence": null, "removedMarker": null, "correction": {"A": "was", "B": "whatever", "C": "done"}, "suggestedCorrection": null, "hasDeliberateError": true}, "hasDeliberateError": true, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: (A)(B)(C) 네모 어법. 정답 ②. 옵션표는 OCR 손실(<그림>/<표>)이나 어법상 정답 조합은 결정 가능: (A) was('One of the exercises...was') / (B) whatever(명사절) / (C) done(수동, 'Being born was done to me')."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q22", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [22], "type": "어법", "answer": 5, "text": "Gas stations are a good example of an impersonal attitude. At many stations, attendants have even stopped pumping gas. Motorists pull up to a gas station where an attendant is enclosed in a glass booth with a tray for taking money. The driver must get out of the car, pump the gas, and walk over to the booth to pay. And customers with engine trouble or a non-functioning heater are usually out of luck. Why? Many gas stations have gotten rid of on-duty mechanics. The skillful mechanic has been replaced by a teenager in a uniform who doesn't know anything about cars and couldn't care less.", "wordCount": 106, "reconstructionKind": "grammar_error", "reconstruction": {"kind": "grammar_error", "blankFilledWith": null, "order": null, "insertedAt": null, "insertedSentence": null, "removedSentence": null, "removedMarker": null, "correction": {"marker": "⑤", "from": "which", "to": "who"}, "suggestedCorrection": null, "hasDeliberateError": true}, "hasDeliberateError": true, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 어법상 틀린 것. 정답 ⑤ which → who(선행사 a teenager, 사람). 밑줄 ①~⑤ 마커 제거, 정답 교정 반영."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q23", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [23], "type": "무관한문장", "answer": 3, "text": "Doubtless, the capacity for contact has a determining influence on health. People with greater capacity for contact have a stronger immune system than those less able to establish relationships with others. One study directly measured individuals' sociability in relation to the efficiency of their immune systems. Questionnaires and interviews given to 334 people examined their sociability―the quantity and quality of their relationships in everyday life. These people were then exposed to a common cold virus. It was found that the more sociable a person was, the less subject he was to contagion.", "wordCount": 92, "reconstructionKind": "irrelevant", "reconstruction": {"kind": "irrelevant", "blankFilledWith": null, "order": null, "insertedAt": null, "insertedSentence": null, "removedSentence": "Researchers didn't know how to obtain a representative sample of the population.", "removedMarker": "③", "correction": null, "suggestedCorrection": null, "hasDeliberateError": false}, "hasDeliberateError": false, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 전체 흐름과 관계 없는 문장. 정답 ③ 삭제(연구가 대표표본 추출법을 몰랐다는 무관 문장). 각주 *contagion 제거, ①~⑤ 마커 제거."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q24", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [24], "type": "빈칸추론", "answer": 5, "text": "Magicians are honest deceivers. To investigate the secret used by magicians to fool their audiences, Jastrow worked with two great illusionists. He invited these performers to his laboratory and had them participate in a range of tests measuring their speed of movement and accuracy of finger motion. But Jastrow's results revealed little out of the ordinary. He demonstrated magic has little to do with fast movements. Instead, magicians use a range of psychological weapons to fool their audiences. The technique of suggestion, which captures people's minds, plays a key role in the process. In the same way that people can be made to believe that they once went on a non-existent trip in a hot-air balloon, so magicians have to be able to manipulate people's perception of performance.", "wordCount": 128, "reconstructionKind": "blank", "reconstruction": {"kind": "blank", "blankFilledWith": "psychological", "order": null, "insertedAt": null, "insertedSentence": null, "removedSentence": null, "removedMarker": null, "correction": null, "suggestedCorrection": null, "hasDeliberateError": false}, "hasDeliberateError": false, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 빈칸 추론. 정답 ⑤ psychological. 문제지 [24~27] 라벨이 실제 번호와 다른 OCR 표기였으나 정답키/내용으로 24번 확정."}
{"passageId": "2009_06_3001198-q25", "examId": "2009_06_3001198", "year": 2009, "exam": "6월", "form": "", "board": "수능모의평가", "era": "foreign_pdf", "qNumbers": [25], "type": "빈칸추론", "answer": 3, "text": "In traditional societies, high status may have been extremely hard to acquire, but it was also comfortingly hard to lose. It was as difficult to stop being a lord as, more darkly, it was to cease being a servant. What mattered was one's identity at birth, rather than anything one might achieve in one's lifetime through the exercise of one's abilities. The great aspiration of modern societies, however, has been to reverse this equation―to strip away both inherited privilege and inherited under-privilege in order to make rank dependent on individual achievement. Status in the current society rarely depends on an unchangeable identity handed down through the generations.", "wordCount": 107, "reconstructionKind": "blank", "reconstruction": {"kind": "blank", "blankFilledWith": "an unchangeable identity", "order": null, "insertedAt": null, "insertedSentence": null, "removedSentence": null, "removedMarker": null, "correction": null, "suggestedCorrection": null, "hasDeliberateError": false}, "hasDeliberateError": false, "confidence": "high", "note": "발문: 빈칸 추론. 정답 ③ an unchangeable identity."}
